In my experience, Excalibur is one of the two best artifact
weapons you can have.  Snickersnee is a powerful weapon, but
without any of the added benefits of Excalibur or Grayswandir
(which is even better than Excalibur).  If you're loaded with
?EW, charge up Snickersnee a bit now, for the added benefit
until you've gotten one of the others, but plan on using either
Grayswandir or Excalibur in the long run.  (Note that as a
Samura=C3=AF, Grayswandir isn't that cool in the beginning, since you
can only get sabre to basic, and will still be missing from time
to time.  As you advance, however, you'll get to a level where
you'll never miss, even at basic.)

Whichever you have, dual weapon with your original katana (or
later, possibly with a silver sabre, especially if you have
Excalibur, rather than Grayswandir).

And don't forget your bow and arrows for ranged attacts.  Find
some normal arrows for practice (don't waste your ya).  Once
you've maxed luck and blessed the ya, you can use them very
effectively at distance, with minimal losses.  (For maximum
effectiveness, get your bow skills up to expert---even before
advancing long sword or two weapon beyond skilled.)

